# Java coding standards

Target **Java 11**. Do not use records, text blocks, switch expressions, or APIs newer than 11.

## Class shape

- Utility / factory types are `public final` with a **private constructor**: `DriverFactory`, `ConfigReader`, `WaitUtils`, `ScreenshotUtils`, `LoginDataProvider`.
- Page objects are concrete classes extending `BasePage`. Tests extend `BaseTest`.
- No Lombok, Guice, or Spring. No `var` in new framework code unless a nearby file already uses it (current sources do not).
- Keep fields `private`. Locators are `private static final By`.
- Do not introduce shared mutable statics other than `ConfigReader`'s properties and `DriverFactory`'s `ThreadLocal`.

## Naming

| Kind | Pattern | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| Page class | `<Screen>Page` | `CheckoutInfoPage` |
| Test class | `<Area>Tests` | `CartTests` |
| Test method | `should<Behavior>` | `shouldLoginWithValidCredentials` |
| Locator | `UPPER_SNAKE` | `LOGIN_BUTTON` |
| Constants | `UPPER_SNAKE` | `STANDARD_USER` |
| Packages | existing `com.automation.*` | do not create `com.saucedemo` |

## Style

- Explicit imports; no `import org.openqa.selenium.*` except where a file already needs many Selenium types.
- 4-space indent; braces on the same style as neighboring files.
- One public top-level class per file.
- Prefer existing typed accessors (`ConfigReader.getBaseUrl()`) over `getProperty("baseUrl")` in new code.
- Fail fast with `IllegalStateException` / `RuntimeException` like `DriverFactory.getDriver()` and `ConfigReader` — **custom exception types do not exist**.

## Dependencies

Do not add libraries for problems already solved (`WaitUtils`, WebDriverManager, Allure). If Java 11 forces a verbose construct, keep it verbose rather than bumping the compiler level.
